; SD data tables (reference only; DATA, not code):
; 0x4867B9A4  DiskWorkerTaskDesc     ; MILK task descriptor {0,1,DiskWorkerTask,3,0xC00}
; 0x4867B9CC  SdCmd10Frame           ; {3,1,4A 00 00 00 00} = CMD10 SEND_CID
; 0x4867B9D8  SdCmd9Frame            ; {3,1,49 00 00 00 00} = CMD9 SEND_CSD
; 0x4867B9E4  SdCmd16Frame           ; {3,1,50 00 00 02 00} = CMD16 SET_BLOCKLEN 0x200
; 0x4867B9F0  DriveCtrlJumpTable     ; 15 x code ptr, drive-ctrl cmd 0x40..0x4E
; 0x4867BA2C  DriveLetterClassTable  ; 14 x code ptr for DriveLetterClass
; 0x4867BA64  SdCmd59BadCrcFrame     ; {3,1,7B 00 00 00 01} = CMD59 CRC_ON, sent with a corrupted CRC by SdCrcSelfTest
; 0x4867BA70  SdCsdBitMaskTables     ; 8 LSB masks + 8 MSB masks for SdCsdBitfield
; 0x4875894C  SdCidShadowInit        ; 16 zero bytes -> 0x50082728
; 0x4875896C  SdCrc7Table            ; 256-byte CRC7 table (poly 0x09<<1)
; The MN10300 host-boots the SHARC and streams effect programs to it (index
; port 0x98000000, data port 0x9C000000). Full analysis in
; kn7000_mame/notes/dsp-effect-catalog.md and dsp-host-interface.md; the SHARC
; programs themselves are disassembled under kn7000_disassembly/disasm/dsp/.
