; ---- TG note path (library image): key event -> note-on -> per-element EG /
;      release programming. RE: kn7000_mame/notes/tg-pitch-pipeline.md +
;      notes/tg-envelope-sweep-results.md. The 0x84-byte record 0x500CA0B0 +
;      slot*0x84 is the SHADOW REGISTER CACHE for the slot's TG regs, as
;      4-byte entries [lo16 = note-on value | hi16 = release value]:
;      +0x00 reg0 [ATK|PEAK], +0x04 reg1 [DCY1|SUS1], +0x08 reg2 [DCY2|SUS2]
;      (+0x0A doubles as the reg3 gate-off value), +0x0C reg4, +0x10 reg5,
;      +0x18 reg8, +0x1C reg9; then +0x24 level, +0x40 zone word, +0x48
;      pitch18, +0x54 class-0x3000 word, +0x5C send word, +0x78/+0x7A/+0x7C/
;      +0x80 dirty masks. -----------------------------------------------------
0x4C0309A5  TgExclGroupChoke        ; (d0 part, d1 new slot) exclusive-group choke: desc(librec+0x38)+0x0E bit7 = in an excl group (id &0x7F -> damp-rate table 0x48586EA4); collect same-part voices via 0x4C01010A, and for each whose desc group matches: release halves of reg0/reg1 (+0x02/+0x06) := damp rate<<8 (levels cleared) then TgVoiceEgBurstWrite -- the hi-hat-style cutoff
0x4C030A84  TgTotalLevelCalc        ; (d0, d1) -> 0x4C00F9B4(d0, d1, 0x40) & 0xFFFF: level/velocity resolve used by the note-on programmers (>= 0x100 result suppresses the effect-send fields)
0x4C030A9D  TgElemNoteOnStd         ; (d0 slot, a0 shadow rec) per-element note-on programmer, standard class (librec+2 bit1): fills the shadow cache -- +0x40 zone word (desc+2 &0xFFF), pitch16 via 0x4C02FB7E then +0x48 pitch18 := ((pitch16+0x1800)<<2)&0x3FFFF (THE pipeline formula), +0x24 level (0x4C02FBE3 &0x7F), effect sends +0x5C/+0x2C from desc2+0x18/+0x19 via curve tables 0x486D1F54/0x486D2154 (skipped when TgTotalLevelCalc >= 0x100), + class-0x04/0x0C global writes
0x4C030E73  TgVoiceKillHandler      ; slot-service class-0x08 handler (d0 slot): clears the lib record's active bit (+8 bit7); when desc+0x0D bit5 is set continues into the 0x50009944 block via 0x4C02FE59 (else plain return)
0x4C030FB9  TgPitchInitCalc         ; the tg-pitch-pipeline notes' INIT pitch computation (note16 -> pitch16 with zone center/exp, coarse/fine, multisample corr); populates librec +0x0C notePitch16 race-free before the first TG write
0x4C031127  TgPitchRuntimeCalc      ; the notes' RUNTIME pitch recompute: init formula + modulation (part offset, mod matrix, LFO, portamento); called from every per-class voice-refresh handler
0x4C031949  TgKeyOffAmpRelease      ; key-off AMPLITUDE release compute (d0 key-off offset, a0 librec, a1 out [rate|lvl]x2): rate index = clamp(desc2+0x2E base + part-FX rec (0x500B5340+n*0x54C)+0x48 RELEASE offset + d0 + key scale (desc2+0x31..0x33 breakpoints vs librec+0xC note), 0..100) -> curve ROM 0x486D2649; out pairs become shadow reg0/reg1 (burst 0x9180/0x9100 on the piano damp) -- STATIC ANSWER to the envelope-sweep RESULT-2 open: screen RLS enters HERE, not the TG regs
0x4C031C50  TgPitchEgAttackCalc    ; running-voice PITCH-EG attack program (a0 librec, a1 desc2): rate desc2+0x0B via curve 0x486D2649, key scale desc2+0x15..0x17 (desc2+0x0B..0x12 = the pitch EG, regs 4..6 per the a1 live decode); called by every class refresh handler
0x4C031D9B  TgPitchEgDecayCalc     ; running-voice PITCH-EG decay program: rates desc2+0x0D/+0x0F via curve 0x486D2649, key scale desc2+0x17
0x4C031F07  TgKeyOffPitchRelease   ; key-off PITCH-EG release compute (a0 librec, a1 out): desc2+0x11 release rate + desc2+0x12 scale via curves 0x486D2649/0x486D2713; out pairs become shadow reg4/reg5 (the piano burst's 0xAE00/0xAE00 = pitch pairs to instant-zero)
0x4C0321BF  TgFilterEgAttackCalc   ; running-voice FILTER-EG attack program: desc2+0x40 rate (>=2 via curve 0x486D2649), desc2+0x4A key scale (desc2+0x3E..0x4C = the filter EG, regs 8..0xA per the a1 live decode)
0x4C03231F  TgFilterEgDecayCalc    ; running-voice FILTER-EG decay program: desc2+0x42/+0x44 rates via curve 0x486D2649, desc2+0x4C
0x4C032490  TgKeyOffFilterRelease  ; key-off FILTER-EG release compute (a0 librec, a1 out): desc2+0x46 rate via 0x486D2649, signed level clamp(desc2+0x47 + desc2+0x3E, -50..50) via 0x486D2713 (desc2+0x3E = the folded CUTOFF ADJUST); out pairs become shadow reg8/reg9 (piano burst 0x22B0: sweep the filter shut to signed level 0xB0)
