;
; ---- melodic ZONE PARAM FETCHERS 0x4C00FD4C..0x4C010042 (the leaf layer
;      under TgElemNoteOnFresh/TgElemNoteOnStd: tone-zone record (desc2, a1)
;      bytes -> the shadow-image level/velocity/send/filter-EG fields; the
;      +-50-index SENSITIVITY CURVE ROM 0x486D2713 converts UI offsets to
;      hardware units, key scaling via the pair 0x486D1354/0x486D13D4;
;      negative zone bytes select the mirrored curve with negated result).
;      The 0x4C011F2F..0x4C012225 set is their BYTE-FOR-BYTE TWIN linked
;      into TgKitElemNoteOn for the drum-kit/table classes. ------------------
0x4C00FD4C  TgZoneParamClamp        ; (d0 value, d1 max, (stack) min) -> d0 clamped to [min,max] (both halfword-signed) -- the shared clamp every fetcher tails into (kit twin 0x4C011F2F)
0x4C00FD4E  TgZoneParamClamp_entry
0x4C00FD68  TgZoneLevelScaleCalc    ; (a0 librec, a1 desc2) -> signed level term: desc2+9 level offset through the sensitivity curve 0x486D2713 (negative -> negated mirror), then if desc2+0x14 key-scale slope nonzero: += slope * key-curve[note&0x7F] (librec+0x10; tables 0x486D1354 down /0x486D13D4 up) >> 6, clamped 0..0x7F -- feeds the shadow +0x16 total-level hi byte
